**-----------------------------------------------------------------------------
** Rate-dependent plasticity, single element  --  Abaqus/Standard
**
**   units : mm - N - tonne - s   (stress MPa)
**   model : same 1 mm cube and 1/8 symmetry as the DP600 quasi-static deck,
**           but pulled on an EXPONENTIAL history so the TRUE strain rate is
**           exactly 100 /s throughout:   u(t) = exp(100 t) - 1
**           t = 0 .. 0.00405465 s  ->  u = 0 .. 0.5 mm
**   check : sigma_x ~= 770.30 MPa , reaction ~= 514.29 N
**           (quasi-static answer 700.32 MPa x the 1.10 rate factor)
**
**   rate law : Cowper-Symonds   sigma = sigma_static * [1 + (eps_dot/D)^(1/n)]
**              D = 1.0e7 /s , n = 5   ->  factor 1.10 at 100 /s
**   Abaqus writes this as *RATE DEPENDENT, TYPE=POWER LAW with (D, n).
**   LS-DYNA calls the same two numbers C and P on *MAT_024; Ansys calls them
**   gamma and m on TB,RATE PERZYNA.  Same law, three names.
**
**   Rate-dependent yield IS active in an Abaqus/Standard *STATIC step -- the
**   docs list it as one of the few time-dependent responses that are.  The
**   step time therefore has physical meaning here and must not be rescaled.
**
**   run   : abaqus job=rate-1elem-abaqus interactive
**-----------------------------------------------------------------------------
*HEADING
Rate-dependent plasticity 1-element, 100/s (mm-N-tonne-s)
*PREPRINT, ECHO=NO, MODEL=NO, HISTORY=NO
